Helm Debugging and Troubleshooting
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Use Helm debug commands to diagnose application issues
Identify and troubleshoot common Helm deployment failures
Resolve Helm chart configuration problems
Implement best practices for Helm debugging
Use Helm testing and validation features
Analyze Helm release history and rollback failed deployments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with YAML syntax
Basic command-line interface experience
Understanding of containerization concepts
Previous experience with Helm basics (installation, charts, releases)
