Step 1: Create a comprehensive debugging checklist

cat << 'EOF' > helm-debug-checklist.md
# Helm Debugging Checklist

## Pre-Installation Checks
- [ ] Chart syntax validation (`helm lint`)
- [ ] Template rendering test (`helm template`)
- [ ] Values file validation
- [ ] Dependencies check (`helm dependency list`)

## Installation Issues
- [ ] Check Helm release status (`helm status`)
- [ ] Verify Kubernetes resources (`kubectl get all`)
- [ ] Check pod status and events (`kubectl describe pods`)
- [ ] Review container logs (`kubectl logs`)
- [ ] Validate resource quotas and limits

## Common Issues to Check
- [ ] Image pull errors (ImagePullBackOff)
- [ ] Resource constraints (CPU/Memory limits)
- [ ] Configuration errors in templates
- [ ] RBAC permission issues
- [ ] Network connectivity problems
- [ ] Persistent volume issues
- [ ] Service discovery problems

## Debugging Commands
```bash
# Template debugging
helm template <release> <chart> --debug --dry-run

# Installation debugging
helm install <release> <chart> --debug --dry-run
helm install <release> <chart> --debug --wait --timeout=300s

# Status and history
helm status <release>
helm history <release>

# Kubernetes debugging
kubectl get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp
kubectl describe pods -l app.kubernetes.io/instance=<release>
kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/instance=<release>
Recovery Actions
 Rollback to previous version (helm rollback)
 Upgrade with fixed configuration (helm upgrade)
 Uninstall and reinstall if necessary
 Check and update dependencies EOF

## Task 7: Best Practices and Prevention

### Subtask 7.1: Implement Chart Validation

**Step 1: Create a chart validation script**

```bash
cat << 'EOF' > validate-chart.sh
#!/bin/bash

CHART_DIR=$1

if [ -z "$CHART_DIR" ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <chart-directory>"
    exit 1
fi

echo "=== Validating Helm Chart: $CHART_DIR ==="

# Check if Chart.yaml exists
if [ ! -f "$CHART_DIR/Chart.yaml" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Chart.yaml not found in $CHART_DIR"
    exit 1
fi

# Lint the chart
echo "Running helm lint..."
helm lint "$CHART_DIR"
LINT_EXIT_CODE=$?

# Test template rendering
echo "Testing template rendering..."
helm template test-release "$CHART_DIR" --debug > /dev/null
TEMPLATE_EXIT_CODE=$?

# Check for common issues
echo "Checking for common issues..."

# Check for hardcoded values
echo "Checking for hardcoded values..."
grep -r "localhost\|127.0.0.1\|hardcoded" "$CHART_DIR/templates/" && echo "WARNING: Found potential hardcoded values"

# Check for missing resource limits
echo "Checking for resource limits..."
if ! grep -r "resources:" "$CHART_DIR/templates/" > /dev/null; then
    echo "WARNING: No resource limits found in templates"
fi

# Summary
echo "=== Validation Summary ==="
if [ $LINT_EXIT_CODE -eq 0 ] && [ $TEMPLATE_EXIT_CODE -eq 0 ]; then
    echo "✓ Chart validation passed"
    exit 0
else
    echo "✗ Chart validation failed"
    exit 1
fi
EOF

chmod +x validate-chart.sh
